---Restart Policies

	--the --restart parameter in docker run allow you to specify a restart policy for the container
		--this is useful for ensuring that containers stay running even if they crash or if the docker daemon restarts
	* docker run -d --name nginx-restart --restart unless-stopped nginx
		---Other policies include
			-no:The default...dont auto restart the container
			-on-failure:Restarts only if the container exits with a non-zero status
			-always:Always restarts the container regardless of the exit status
	* docker inspect -f '{{.HostConfig.RestartPolicy.Name}}' nginx-restart
